WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.736
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:08.685
 They're are arrows more
dangerous than that one?

00:00:08.685 --> 00:00:12.000
 Marvel Studios' Hawkeye
is always on target, thanks

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.765
to VFX supervisor, Greg Steele.

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:14.565
Hey, Greg.

00:00:14.565 --> 00:00:15.420
 Hey, Lorraine.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.260
How are you?

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.160
Thanks for having me today.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.170
 Oh, I am doing excellent.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.240
But, you know, much
like Kate, I am

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.240
dying to know more about
all of the different trick

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.950
arrows in Hawkeye's arsenal.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.050
So how did you and
the production team

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.990
work together to
create these arrows?

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.700
 The props department
is really involved

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.770
in coming up with a lot of
these designs, which is great.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.680
I mean, the work they
did in building these,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.150
they're like little
pieces of artwork

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.280
in terms of the complexity
and the design aesthetic.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.080
It's really great.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.290
And it all lives within
the realm of what's

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.090
come before in the other films.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.580
And the arrows that the
characters were holding

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.170
were not real, but
they were based

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.970
on things the prop
department had put together.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.980
Like the tip of
the PYM arrow had

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.290
a blue illumination and the
word, you could read it.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.200
We scan pretty much everything
we do when we're on the film,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.240
so we'll scan all the locations
and the actors and the props

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.040
also.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.690
You've got the
geometry, which is

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.160
the foundational shape of it.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.380
And then you go in and you
try to replicate the feeling

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.160
of the surface and quality.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.120
So the shininess,
how beat up it is,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.010
where there's little
lights that could turn on,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.120
things like that.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.770
And then you age it and
try and make it look

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.420
like it kind of belongs
in the real world

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.385
versus being totally synthetic.

00:01:23.385 --> 00:01:25.950
 It's definitely a lot
of work, but it's so worth

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.740
it when you see it in
scenes like the epic

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.720
car chase in episode three.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.910
What are some of the different
arrows we see in that scene

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.500
and how did you
bring them to life?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.380
 So, the putty arrow is
one of the first arrows

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.970
that Kate shoots
during the car chase.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.460
Once the arrow hits,
it expands and creates

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.890
this almost like expansion
foam-type quality.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.450
So to create
something like that,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.940
we ended up just shooting the
plate of the truck driving.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.150
And then in post-production,
we did effects simulations

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.380
on the glass.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.160
So they reference material that
we had found of expansion foam

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.500
and some slimes and things
like that that everyone liked.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.960
And then, basically, put it
all together and just kind of

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.450
gave a really kind
of goopy messy look.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.610
The explosive arrow
was one that was

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.860
launched by Kate at the
beginning of the sequence.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.280
It jams into the bumper
of a van and causes

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.100
a giant explosion as
it flips end-over-end,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.870
kind of rolling
towards them almost.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.850
The special effects
team and the stunts team

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.460
rigged up two different
events of a real van.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.890
One was to get it
rolling so it could

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.510
be kind of chasing
along after the car,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.100
and one to get it
going initially.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.620
And then it was up to us in
visual effects to kind of help

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.650
augment that a little bit,
clean up the stunt rigging.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.950
We added some additional fire
and some other explosions

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.490
to kind of just make it all
tie together amongst the shots.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.530
The suction cup
arrow is what appears

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.350
to be a very benign suction
cup arrow at the beginning

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.900
of the sequence, which ends
up actually saving them

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.170
at the end as Clint suction
cup onto a subway car

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.515
as it's speeding below
on the Manhattan bridge.

00:02:52.515 --> 00:02:54.511
 Get the plunger arrow on it.

00:02:54.511 --> 00:02:57.200
 So the Octo-grabber
arrow is an arrow

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.450
device that shoots
cables out from

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.400
itself and then pulls back in.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.760
Kate, basically, fires the arrow
into the front of the truck

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.810
that Cozi's driving.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.840
It spools out all these cables
inside the Christmas lot,

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.120
which they're driving through,
and pulls all the Christmas

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.910
trees causing them to
smash all over the vehicle

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.520
and kind of make them drive
out of control and crash.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.040
We shot all the plates without
Christmas trees in the lot.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.760
So we left space in a Christmas
tree lot dressed with trees

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.350
that the cars could
kind of drive-through

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.850
and the stuntman
can kind of do all

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.440
the action they needed to do.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.960
For most of the shots, we were
putting all these computer

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.670
generated trees that were
built based on some reference

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.470
that we had.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.760
There's some that
are wrapped in,

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.740
encased in kind of
a wrapping, and some

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:37.970
just kind of furled out.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.650
They built those and
then they rigged them up

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.020
so they could simulate such
that if you smashed a tree

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.050
into something, all the branches
and all the pine needles

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.432
would do what
they're supposed to.

00:03:47.432 --> 00:03:48.404
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:48.404 --> 00:03:49.505
 Merry Christmas.

00:03:49.505 --> 00:03:53.210
 So the acid arrow is utilized
when Kate and Clint are

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.090
speeding towards an
intersection with cross traffic

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.340
and they need to, basically,
create a hole in the traffic

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.810
so they can sneak
through it with the guys

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:00.830
chasing after them.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.440
So Clint hands Kate
two acid arrows

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.450
and she's instructed to shoot
them at the traffic lights.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.180
They fly through the air and
they hit a CG traffic light

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.240
pole, it burns away, and they
kind of fall to the ground

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.280
simmering and smoldering.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.519
The PIM arrow, there's
two forms PIM arrows.

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.290
There's the ones that
shrink and then there's

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.880
the ones that grow much larger.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.680
At the end of the
sequence, they're trapped,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.290
the car has been
smashed, and Clint

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.720
tells Kate to take
a regular arrow

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.160
and shoot it up in the sky.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.830
We see that Clint has
got a blue PIM arrow.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.410
And he fires at it as
the arrow is coming down

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.893
and it scales up and chops
the truck basically in half.

00:04:36.893 --> 00:04:38.060
It was something
that we had played

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.920
around with in terms
of how the arrow

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.630
could go through the truck.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.847
I believe it was Kevin
who had the idea.

00:04:43.847 --> 00:04:45.080
He said, no, no,
shoot it straight up

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.460
and then have it
come straight down

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.230
and chop the truck in half.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.700
And it ended up actually
working out really well.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.930
Everything in that
environment is all CG.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.900
So the bridge, the environment
of New York, and all that

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.880
was all basically replicated.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.100
It's a real synergistic
thing between stunts

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.850
and special effects
and visual effects.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.250
That's one of the fun
things about the job

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.410
is actually being able to work
with all the different teams

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.810
to put this together.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.530
 Well, it takes a village.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.660
And just when we think
we've seen it all,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.650
you pull out all of the
stops for that final battle

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.940
in the finale.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.490
Now, what are some of the
arrows that you bring back

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.265
and some of the new arrows that
you introduced for this scene?

00:05:22.265 --> 00:05:24.590
 So the luminous
arrow was, I think,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.560
the first arrow that Kate
shoots inside the ice rink.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.710
And that's basically
a huge blinding light

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.360
just to try to kind
of blind them so they

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.920
can kind of get some cover.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:39.530
I'd say 95% of the shots were
shot in Atlanta on a backlot.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:43.010
For us, it was taking all
the footage that we had shot

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:46.250
and just augmenting what
was a one story building

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.470
and turn it into a
big 65 floor high

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:50.420
rise skyscraper in New York.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.310
The electromagnetic
arrow is something

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.440
that's used at the beginning
of the ice rink fight.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.200
The big question during prep was
when we were kind of designing

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.390
this was why don't all the
bad guys just shoot them

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.650
once they're down
inside the rink?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.720
So we came up with
this gag of Clint

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.510
shooting an electromagnetic
arrow at the flagpole,

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.360
and it basically creates this
electro net all around the ice

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.030
rink and it pulls all of
the metal-based weaponry

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.890
out of the bad
guys' hands and kind

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.990
of sticks it to the flagpoles.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.840
In post, we put in the
electro aspect of it

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.760
with the lightning bolts
and electricity and things

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.910
like that.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.450
So the acid arrow comes back
actually in the final battle.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:26.870
It's before Clint lets Kate
use all the good trick arrows

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.070
when they get down to the ice.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.960
She's basically
up in FAO Schwarz,

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.850
and Clint is stuck in
a tree at this point.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.460
So she, basically, fires
it at the trunk of the tree

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.820
and cause the weight of the
tree to actually fall over.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.040
Clint goes flying,
everything is a hot mess

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.180
down on the ice rink.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.340
Special effects built
us a special tree trunk

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.750
that we could actually crack.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.150
Our vendor team
put in a the acid

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.580
that was eating away
at it, causing bubbles

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.720
and smoke coming off it.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.210
And then the tree itself
as that falls just

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.790
has a massive amount of
stimulation going on.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.460
Kate fires the needle
arrow towards a place

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.650
where a bunch of tracksuit
mafia are standing.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.330
So she fires it,
it hits the ice,

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.930
and winds up small
needles, like a porcupine,

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:08.210
go flying out of this thing and
just stabbing into all the guys

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.310
around it, just kind of
causing mayhem, basically,

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:11.390
at the beginning of the fight.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:15.050
The actual final effect was
designed during post-vis

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.910
as we were doing it.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.600
We had the actual plates and
we just basically implemented

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.000
a CG version of that
shooting until all

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.380
the actors who
were miming getting

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.750
hit by the different needles.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.810
The tranq arrow is an arrow that
is a delivery system yet again.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:33.170
So the main arrow goes
into a guy's shoulder,

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:35.163
so it's just a bunch of
little hypodermic needles

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:36.530
that shoot into the
different characters.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.380
But the performances, again,
for something like that

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.290
is really what sell it.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.380
The airbag, again, is one
of those great combinations

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.160
between stunts and visual
effects and second unit teams.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.010
It was something the stunts
team came up with in their stunt

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.630
biz about this concept of a cool
air-bag that could kind of go

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:57.810
under the characters
and grow huge and send

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.890
them flying into the air.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.530
To actually implement
that, the stunt team set up

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.360
a bunch of cranes and they
could kind of actually

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.350
pull the characters
up into the air.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.410
So we were able to
actually use real people

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.780
doing the stunts versus
having to go to a digit double

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.920
all the time.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.310
The sonic concussion arrow is an
arrow that first gets revealed

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.950
in episode 4, and
that's basically

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.860
an arrow that
creates a large kind

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:23.220
of a three-beat
concussive sonic blast.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:27.390
So, again, we used similar
techniques to what we had done,

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:30.180
creating these
concentric compressed air

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.860
simulations to kind
of just make it feel

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.110
very powerful and concussive.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.970
The giant explosion
arrow that kind of

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.710
happens at the end of
the ice rink sequence

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.270
is very similar to the one
that took out the van earlier.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.840
But for the most part,
the lighting teams created

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.430
some interactive light for us.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.140
The stunt team rigged
up some performers

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.330
to come flying through the
air, get up off the ground,

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.700
and get pulled by these cables
and come flying forward.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.220
Visual effects-wise, we ended
up adding all the explosion

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.990
and the debris that would fly.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.490
The splitting of
the regular arrow.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.530
So Clint's down to two
arrows with three bad guys

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.330
coming at him.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:03.480
So what he does is he fires
one and then quickly fires

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.700
another one with
greater force, causing

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.640
that second arrow to cut
through the first arrow,

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.510
splitting it in half.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.520
So he basically
creates three arrows.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.490
We created all the camera
movement in computer graphics.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.470
We had our virtual
set so we could

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.990
put them anywhere and just kind
of move the camera through it.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.260
So we chased along behind
the arrow in animation

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.510
and split it, added
effect simulations,

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.430
and things like that
to make it very clear

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.380
that it's a wooden arrow.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.170
The PIM arrow comes back
again in the ice rink fight,

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.370
but this time
instead of actually

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:36.360
making something gigantic, it's
used to shrink down something.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.730
And there's several
tracksuit mafia

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.000
that are careening a big
truck into the ice rink

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.780
to try to kind of smash Kate and
Clint as a last ditch effort.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.490
And as it's coming
towards them, Kate

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:51.120
pulls out a PIM shrinking
arrow and fires it at the van,

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.770
shrinking it down.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:55.830
We shot as much as we could
with the actors in the frame,

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.420
but a lot of their
shots ended up just

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:00.180
being fully computer-generated
with the trucks barreling

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.000
across the Plaza because we
had built our CG environment,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.040
we could just drive our
CG trucks through it.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.840
We had computer
generated people standing

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.220
down there as the truck
hurtles towards them.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.000
So after that moment, Kate
turns to Clint and says,

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.330
well, I wasn't really expecting
it to end that way-type thing.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.180
This kind of odd moment where
an owl comes in and takes

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.912
that little truck away.

00:10:19.912 --> 00:10:21.120
 Well, there goes that.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.930
 Now, was that a real owl
or was it something that you

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.850
had to create in post with CGI?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.500
 It was a CG owl.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.480
It was Kevin's idea to
have the owl in the tree.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.850
You obviously read about the
owl that was in the Rockefeller

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:34.650
tree that year.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:35.640
And they called it Rocky.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.140
So that's what we've
called our little owl.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.870
And she's really small,
she's only about yay big,

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:43.050
and she looks just
like the real one.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.300
And it was a very specific type,
so we matched pretty much all

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.860
the feathering and
everything to make it

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.750
look as authentic as possible.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.100
But she's very adorable.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:50.900
[LAUGHTER]

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.140
 That she is.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.840
And now looking back
at this entire series,

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.240
what was your favorite
part of working on it?

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:00.240
 I mean, the content
itself is amazing.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:03.930
One of the original Avengers,
his storyline, and handing

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.490
the mantle over to Kate Bishop.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:08.010
It's a really cool
storyline that we're all

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.690
very excited to be working on.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.390
Everyone's kind of at their
A-game on these projects.

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:14.430
And it's really neat
to be able to kind

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.317
of collaborate with them.

00:11:15.317 --> 00:11:16.650
That's probably one
of my favorite parts

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:17.610
of the whole process.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.710
 Teamwork makes the dream work.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.390
Thank you so much, Greg.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.640
And, of course, go check
out all of those trick

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.620
arrows in Marvel
Studios' Hawkeye,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:30.230
now streaming all episodes
only on Disney Plus.

